{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and the store’s "},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all-or-nothing"}]},{"text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cancel id"}]},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" effect or the imperative "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Identity lives outside the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","text":"Choosing an id"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A cancel id is any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain."}]},{"anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from inside a reducer"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Return ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to tag the work, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to stop it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its "},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","level":2,"anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelInFlight: true"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels any effect already running under the id "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:"}]},{"code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".queryChanged"},{"text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from view or scene code","level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","text":"What it does not replace","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" continuation should still release it — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"type":"text","text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has to stop the effect early."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true,"title":"How-to Guides"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Cancel Effects","roleHeading":"Article"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration."}],"title":"Add iCloud Sync","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"title":"Add Analytics","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancel(id:)":{"title":"cancel(id:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An effect that cancels every in-flight effect running under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancel(id:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels all in-flight effects."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleffects()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancelEffects","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"title":"cancelEffects()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"title":"Add Persistence","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"title":"Add Feature Flags","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"title":"Add a Version Killswitch","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"title":"Effect","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"topic","title":"Add a Paywall","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Tags an effect with a cancellation identity so it can later be cancelled by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.cancel(id:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancellable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancelInFlight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelinflight:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancel(id:)":{"title":"cancel(id:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/cancel(id:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "}